save(k,t,dict(changes=cs,decisions=ds,inventory=ivs,notes='Pencil page 13, no manuscript page number. This page continues “Par construction, tout completed-C_0-morphisme” from scan 012, rather than the unfinished sentence on scan 013. It gives (18)–(22), the factorization through a C_0-morphism and a completed isomorphism, a uniqueness criterion, and a composition recipe. The upper marginal note asserts conservativity and describes completed isomorphisms. It writes a hatted f_0 even in the test for a C_0-isomorphism; the hat is retained. The lower marginal note warns “Il faut savoir interpréter ... déjà la relation” as membership in the completed stabilizer. Its product group is visibly Aut(X)×Aut(Y), although for the displayed u:Y′→Y the first factor would be Aut(Y′); the clear X is retained. The diagram’s two lifts carry literal question marks. The final algebraic rearrangement checks once phi-hat u=u psi-hat is supplied; this calculation does not by itself establish the stabilizer-completion identification. The apparent prefix on morphisme comes from the slanted marginal formula overlapping that line, not an epi prefix.',doubts=[['upper NB, cancelled phrase',r'\deleted{De \unsure{plus}}','The second cancelled word lies under the live replacement plus.','low'],['(20) cancelled label',r'\deleted{\unsure{g}}','Dense hatching obscures the original letter.','low'],['before w',r'\deleted{$\unsure{u}$}','The cancelled symbol is only partly visible.','low'],['(22), cancelled letter',r'\deleted{\unsure{g}}','A descender survives but the upper letter is crossed.','low']],hand=[['Slanted marginal text overlaps main baseline','The marginal Aut formula overlaps morphisme in the upper paragraph; this is not a prefix.','C left morphisme/épimorphisme doubtful.'],['psi versus phi-prime','The lift has a trident form at every occurrence on this page; no prime is present.','H repeatedly substituted phi-prime.'],['Source question marks in diagrams','Both diagonal lifts in (21) are followed by question marks.','H omitted both.']],notation=[['hat psi / hat phi','Two distinct lifted automorphisms; psi has two arms, phi a loop.'],['C and C_0','The category after toute flèche is plain C, even though the context suggests C_0.'],['Aut(X) in lower NB','Clear X preserved although the displayed u has domain Y′.']],abbreviations=[['can','canonique'],['iso','isomorphisme'],['Flisom.','flèches isomorphismes']],checks=[check('142-014-product','(22)','(v g_0)(u f_0)=(vwu)(psi f_0) if g_0=w phi and phi u=u psi.','Verified by substitution and associativity: v(w phi)u f_0 = vw(phi u)f_0 = vwu(psi f_0). The source cancellation does not affect the live formula.','computation or formal certificate'),check('142-014-domain','lower NB','The stabilizer of u:Y′→Y acts through Aut(Y′)×Aut(Y).','Checked domains of phi u and u psi: psi must act on Y′. The source’s Aut(X) is retained and noted as a local variable mismatch.'),check('142-014-conservative','upper NB','The completion functor is conservative and has the asserted completed Isom spaces.','Recorded as the author’s assertion in this note; not independently proved in this run.','carried as background without fault found'),check('142-014-lift','lower NB','The relation phi u=u psi is equivalent to membership in completed G_u.','Recorded as a point the author explicitly says must be interpreted; the algebraic calculation assumes it and does not prove it.','carried as background without fault found')]))
